D['24303097']=dict(
 title="A Lean-certified conditional implication for the 3D incompressible Navier–Stokes equations: Hypothesis B and the Beale–Kato–Majda criterion imply global regularity of maximal classical solutions",
 description=COPY+
 "<p>This paper states only what the Lean 4 kernel certificate proves. The Lean-certified results are conditional. (1) ClassicalNS.analyticBridge_of_formB_forall: for every bound C_star, if Hypothesis B holds for C_star and the named Beale–Kato–Majda hypothesis BKMCriterion holds, then for every ν &gt; 0 and every smooth, periodic, divergence-free initial datum, every maximal classical solution of periodic incompressible Navier–Stokes is global (T* = ⊤) and has finite ∫₀ᵀ ‖∇u(t)‖_{L∞} dt for every finite T &gt; 0. (2) ClassicalNS.formB_Hs_bound: under the same hypotheses plus the named hypothesis KatoPonceEnergy, HsR(s, u(t)) ≤ HsR(s, u₀) exp(C_s max(C_star(T), 0)) on [0, T]. Hypothesis B, BKMCriterion and KatoPonceEnergy are assumptions, not theorems of the development. Both results are under Truth Gate locks (paper source SHA-256 e8723c81b7d94f595b053e8e260c8037f349960951a6612f18b98b73f46703f4).</p>"
 +OPEN+
 "<p>Not formalized and not claimed: Kato local existence, Fujita–Kato small-data global regularity, a strain-only continuation criterion, logarithmic Sobolev bounds, a parabolic bootstrap, the Beale–Kato–Majda criterion itself, and the geometric metriplectic completion as a derivation of Navier–Stokes on 𝕋³. Their formalization is left open.</p>"
 +CERT+
 "<p>Files: Frohmanian_Tether_Unified.pdf (primary manuscript), its LaTeX source Frohmanian_Tether_Unified.tex (byte-identical to the file at the certifying commit), references.bib, the certificate stamp and block, and Frohmanian_Tether_Unified_build.tex, the build entry point that inputs the unchanged source and changes typesetting only (a monospace font with the Unicode symbols in Lean names, and line breaks in long identifiers). MANIFEST_tether.txt lists the SHA-256 of every file. NOTICE asks for citation.</p>"
 "<p>Version note. This version supersedes v1.2 (10.5281/zenodo.24301283). v1.2 deposited a hand-written CI_RUN summary instead of an official kernel certificate, was built from a Lean tree whose open target was a theorem proved by sorry, and stated Kato local existence and Fujita–Kato small-data global regularity as theorems although they are not formalized in Lean. This version removes those claims, records the open target as a proposition with no proof, and deposits the official certificate. The companion audit of legacy formalization defects is 10.5281/zenodo.24102968; the companion note 10.5281/zenodo.24080309 records the same conditional implication. This work is strictly conditional and does not resolve the Clay Millennium Problem.</p>",
 drop_related=['https://github.com/BenFrohman/NS_Millennium_Proof'])
